operators: operator is a symbol that used to perform operations on values or on a variables 
ex:
a=10
b=20
print(a+b)
here "+" ia an operator


types of operators:

1.arithmetic operators: used for mathematical operations

which are: 
+ : add
- : sub
* : mul
/ : div
% : modulus 
** : power 


2.relational operators : these are used to compare values 
which are:
==
!=
>
<
>=
<=
 ex: 
a=10
b=15
print(a>b)


3.logical operator : 
and - both  conditions are must be true
or - any one condition can true
not - opposite result

ex: 
age = 20
print(age>18 and <25)


4.assignment operators: used to assign values 

